WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:07.860
You touched my hand when I stretched them out so far...

00:00:19.330 --> 00:00:21.660
Just one word is fine.

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:24.500
Just voice your dreams.

00:00:24.750 --> 00:00:28.630
It's your first step and first sign to realization.

00:00:30.170 --> 00:00:32.720
Ask yourself what is it that you like?

00:00:33.010 --> 00:00:34.840
Your answers will...

00:00:34.840 --> 00:00:39.850
blow your questions high into the sky.

00:00:35.590 --> 00:00:36.260
Even more...

00:00:37.050 --> 00:00:38.140
Like fireworks...

00:00:39.850 --> 00:00:46.350
Even though we should all try to be more honest we ourselves, we can't.

00:00:46.650 --> 00:00:53.360
Maybe I should try summoning my soul as a child?

00:00:53.860 --> 00:00:59.910
What touched my hand when i stretched them out so far...

00:01:00.030 --> 00:01:05.040
was a Supernova that suddenly appear to this new night.

00:01:05.160 --> 00:01:11.000
For millions of light years, it never stops inside of me.

00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:19.220
The longer I gaze, the more power my eyes absorb...

00:01:19.220 --> 00:01:24.480
and that's because... because I'm a star too!

00:01:26.020 --> 00:01:31.020
The oh-so-fun summer camp is over,

00:01:26.020 --> 00:01:31.020
carving "summer memories" into everyone's heart.

00:01:31.020 --> 00:01:36.030
A lot of stuff happened on the way back,

00:01:31.020 --> 00:01:36.030
but that is yet another story.

00:01:42.240 --> 00:01:43.160
Saku!

00:01:44.160 --> 00:01:45.710
Saku, wake up!

00:01:46.540 --> 00:01:47.330
It's morning!

00:01:48.580 --> 00:01:49.130
Good morning.

00:01:51.670 --> 00:01:52.000
What?

00:01:53.670 --> 00:01:55.510
You could have at least slept in today.

00:01:55.630 --> 00:01:55.970
What?

00:01:56.090 --> 00:01:57.260
Saku, you meanie!

00:01:57.550 --> 00:01:59.640
Do you enjoy spoiling Mom's fun?

00:01:59.760 --> 00:02:00.680
Geez...

00:02:00.930 --> 00:02:03.770
Why can't you act more like a teenager?!

00:02:03.770 --> 00:02:04.850
What the hell is wrong with you this early in the morning?!

00:02:04.930 --> 00:02:05.810
Papa!

00:02:05.810 --> 00:02:06.930
Papa, save me!

00:02:07.270 --> 00:02:10.190
Our son is growing up!

00:02:10.230 --> 00:02:12.070
Don't call him over something like that!

00:02:16.440 --> 00:02:17.530
The first of September.

00:02:18.030 --> 00:02:18.700
A new school term.

00:02:19.950 --> 00:02:21.820
My summer vacation went by really quickly this year.

00:02:23.580 --> 00:02:27.250
Somehow, I feel as though a lot more happened this year than previous years.

00:02:28.040 --> 00:02:31.460
Is it just because I'm allowed to do more things now that I'm in high school?

00:02:32.210 --> 00:02:32.840
Or...

00:02:37.380 --> 00:02:38.550
Saku-chan!

00:02:38.630 --> 00:02:40.340
Saku-chan!

00:02:39.010 --> 00:02:40.300
I guess a lot did happen.

00:02:41.840 --> 00:02:44.060
The next stop is Souei High School.

00:02:44.180 --> 00:02:45.640
Souei High School.

00:02:56.900 --> 00:03:01.530
T-This must be the bell battle that occurs from time to time amongst bus commuters!

00:03:02.370 --> 00:03:03.830
Since a lot of people get off at the same bus stop,

00:03:03.830 --> 00:03:06.450
everyone believes that someone else will press the bell for them.

00:03:06.490 --> 00:03:07.500
And before you know it, you're engulfed in an eerie tense atmosphere,

00:03:07.540 --> 00:03:09.250
and it becomes a stand-off as no one dares press it!

00:03:10.120 --> 00:03:11.080
What should I do?

00:03:11.540 --> 00:03:13.420
If I'm going to press it, I should do it soon.

00:03:13.960 --> 00:03:14.750
What should I do?

00:03:15.250 --> 00:03:16.090
What should I do?

00:03:23.850 --> 00:03:24.760
I... can't press it.

00:03:27.720 --> 00:03:29.140
Stopping at the next bus stop.

00:03:48.240 --> 00:03:49.790
He's huge.

00:03:53.710 --> 00:03:55.000
A blond Mokomichi!

00:03:53.710 --> 00:03:55.630
[Note: Mokomichi Hayami is a Japanese actor and model.]

00:03:55.630 --> 00:03:57.250
He looks like Mokomichi!

00:03:57.670 --> 00:04:01.550
His hair has grown longer, but he still looks like Mokomichi!

00:04:02.470 --> 00:04:05.260
Hasn't she changed <i>a lot</i> over summer vacation?

00:04:05.720 --> 00:04:08.390
T-Takagi-san, did something happen?

00:04:08.810 --> 00:04:10.770
You've got a tan.

00:04:10.770 --> 00:04:12.350
I'm a lot paler than I was before.

00:04:12.350 --> 00:04:14.900
Tada! Here are your souvenirs, apple chips.

00:04:16.650 --> 00:04:21.280
Ooyagi, we failed to join your world...

00:04:21.280 --> 00:04:22.570
Don't draw those lines...

00:04:22.570 --> 00:04:22.950
Wait!

00:04:23.650 --> 00:04:24.990
Saku-chan!

00:04:25.490 --> 00:04:28.740
Look! Look! The photos we took together at night are ready!

00:04:31.250 --> 00:04:32.250
Please show them to us!

00:04:33.870 --> 00:04:36.540
Don't come here first thing in the new term!

00:04:36.710 --> 00:04:38.500
Hime-chan, good morning!

00:04:38.800 --> 00:04:40.920
Don't touch me!

00:04:41.210 --> 00:04:43.510
Look! We were able to take proper photographs!

00:04:44.430 --> 00:04:47.720
I don't want to phrase it this way, but... I'm surprised we managed to take photos of them.

00:04:48.050 --> 00:04:49.470
Why not?

00:04:50.430 --> 00:04:52.890
If they're planets or bright skies, such as the breaking of dawn,

00:04:53.020 --> 00:04:54.730
I'm able to photograph them using a simple compact digital camera.

00:04:56.100 --> 00:04:58.560
Huh? What's this?

00:04:59.110 --> 00:04:59.730
Is it blurred?

00:05:00.150 --> 00:05:01.280
No, no.

00:05:01.280 --> 00:05:02.030
These are stars too.

00:05:02.690 --> 00:05:04.280
It's because the stars are moving.

00:05:04.900 --> 00:05:07.780
The longer the exposure time, the longer the lines get.

00:05:08.200 --> 00:05:08.910
I see.

00:05:09.700 --> 00:05:12.910
Then, what is this faint green thing?

00:05:13.790 --> 00:05:17.500
It must be the city lights from the other side of the mountain.

00:05:18.540 --> 00:05:21.800
It's called light pollution; it's a known problem.

00:05:21.800 --> 00:05:22.340
Yup, yup.

00:05:22.380 --> 00:05:24.420
Even though it was so dark outside?

00:05:25.970 --> 00:05:29.390
Oh, that's right. We need to thank the Photography Club for these.

00:05:29.470 --> 00:05:31.060
Er... No, it's okay.

00:05:31.060 --> 00:05:32.810
Your kind thoughts are all I need!

00:05:36.520 --> 00:05:42.650
It's our duty to photograph transient periods of girls in swimsuits.

00:05:40.360 --> 00:05:42.690
Red box: Half of the Photography Club's kindness is due to an ulterior motive.

00:05:43.320 --> 00:05:46.150
But somehow, part of my dream came true.

00:05:46.780 --> 00:05:48.990
From now on, let's continue to do lots of other fun things.

00:05:49.280 --> 00:05:54.160
It's good to have ideals, but are you sure you're being realistic?

00:05:55.250 --> 00:05:58.540
Requesting an increase in club financing so early into the new term...

00:05:58.790 --> 00:06:01.170
Did you really think I'd okay it?

00:06:01.250 --> 00:06:02.460
Fumin!

00:06:02.630 --> 00:06:06.340
Didn't we confess our love for one another this summer?

00:06:06.590 --> 00:06:07.680
What are you talking about?

00:06:07.720 --> 00:06:09.010
This is ridiculous.

00:06:09.340 --> 00:06:10.640
Therefore, your request is denied.

00:06:12.310 --> 00:06:13.680
Fumin!

00:06:12.430 --> 00:06:13.600
Kotodzuka-senpai?

00:06:13.850 --> 00:06:16.810
Don't abandon us!

00:06:14.270 --> 00:06:16.020
S-She's giving me the chills...

00:06:17.270 --> 00:06:18.980
This is undoubtedly...

00:06:19.440 --> 00:06:21.480
the "Summer Non-uniform Clothes Effect!"

00:06:21.860 --> 00:06:23.110
Is this a summer day's mirage?

00:06:23.270 --> 00:06:25.320
Mysteriously so tight!

00:06:26.030 --> 00:06:26.440
What?

00:06:28.610 --> 00:06:31.240
It makes me really happy...

00:06:31.700 --> 00:06:34.540
...to see the faces of each student...

00:06:34.790 --> 00:06:36.750
...at the start of the new term.

00:06:37.370 --> 00:06:41.630
Somehow, you all seem as though you've matured.

00:06:39.330 --> 00:06:42.130
Principal, Roma-kun has fainted due to nausea.

00:06:41.630 --> 00:06:43.170
This is most likely because you've all spent...

00:06:43.590 --> 00:06:48.220
...your summer days studying hard and playing.

00:06:46.420 --> 00:06:48.010
Oh yeah, where's Yoshikawa?

00:06:48.260 --> 00:06:48.670
I don't know.

00:06:49.380 --> 00:06:54.060
And though my greeting has been short, I shall now bring it to an end.

00:06:54.430 --> 00:06:56.100
It was <i>long</i>.

00:06:58.810 --> 00:07:01.850
Next, we'll be welcoming our new teacher.

00:07:02.730 --> 00:07:05.110
Souma-sensei, please enter.

00:07:18.120 --> 00:07:20.410
I will be teaching history in place of Yoshikawa-sensei,

00:07:21.000 --> 00:07:22.330
who's currently on leave;

00:07:22.710 --> 00:07:23.960
I will also be taking over as Class 1-2's homeroom teacher.

00:07:24.420 --> 00:07:25.420
My name is Souma Nozomu.

00:07:26.800 --> 00:07:27.920
Pleased to meet you.

00:07:30.130 --> 00:07:30.720
He's the guy from this morning.

00:07:32.130 --> 00:07:33.800
What happened to Yoshikawa?

00:07:32.300 --> 00:07:35.100
Class 1-2 is our class!

00:07:33.800 --> 00:07:35.100
Is it true that he quit?

00:07:35.470 --> 00:07:39.560
Since I'm bad at introductions, I'll keep it short.

00:07:40.020 --> 00:07:41.140
However, if you have any questions-

00:07:41.190 --> 00:07:42.020
Sou-nii?

00:07:42.400 --> 00:07:42.770
What?

00:07:46.570 --> 00:07:47.780
Sou-nii?

00:07:52.990 --> 00:07:55.620
Mihoshi... chan?

00:07:57.870 --> 00:07:58.910
Sou-nii!

00:08:02.370 --> 00:08:03.250
Arrest her!

00:08:04.630 --> 00:08:05.710
Quiet down.

00:08:06.340 --> 00:08:07.500
Quiet down.

00:08:08.000 --> 00:08:08.960
Quiet!

00:08:10.420 --> 00:08:14.010
Say, did Mihoshi-senpai have an older brother?

00:08:14.590 --> 00:08:15.180
No...

00:08:29.780 --> 00:08:30.610
My name is Souma Nozomu.

00:08:30.990 --> 00:08:31.990
Thirty years old. Single.

00:08:32.780 --> 00:08:35.070
I was doing volunteer work overseas until last month.

00:08:35.740 --> 00:08:37.530
I believe I have a lot to learn.

00:08:37.830 --> 00:08:38.660
Pleased to meet you.

00:08:39.620 --> 00:08:40.330
Any questions?

00:08:42.040 --> 00:08:44.870
What's with this strange atmosphere...

00:08:44.870 --> 00:08:48.090
Nope, we have no questions...

00:08:48.210 --> 00:08:49.840
Right, Ooyagi?

00:08:50.050 --> 00:08:51.380
Stop it!

00:08:53.130 --> 00:08:53.630
Oh?

00:08:54.090 --> 00:08:56.010
Didn't we bump into each other on the bus this morning?

00:08:56.090 --> 00:08:57.970
They've already had it out this morning?!

00:08:58.180 --> 00:09:00.350
As I said, exactly what <i>is</i> this atmosphere?

00:09:01.060 --> 00:09:03.230
Excuse me... but about what happened earlier...

00:09:03.850 --> 00:09:06.520
What's your relationship with Akeno-senpai?

00:09:07.150 --> 00:09:08.400
What is it? Do you know her?

00:09:10.230 --> 00:09:11.900
She's a senior in the same club.

00:09:12.400 --> 00:09:13.150
The Astronomy Club.

00:09:13.400 --> 00:09:14.240
The Astronomy Club?

00:09:15.490 --> 00:09:16.530
I see. I see.

00:09:16.700 --> 00:09:17.780
She hasn't changed at all.

00:09:18.240 --> 00:09:20.370
Sensei, please answer the question.

00:09:20.990 --> 00:09:21.740
Let's see...

00:09:22.330 --> 00:09:24.000
The head teacher just told me off,

00:09:24.580 --> 00:09:26.500
so I'll just say it's a private matter.

00:09:27.080 --> 00:09:29.130
After all, she's my angel.

00:09:32.960 --> 00:09:33.710
Now then,

00:09:34.130 --> 00:09:36.220
I've got some hand-outs that need distributing.

00:09:36.840 --> 00:09:38.430
Any volunteers?

00:09:38.930 --> 00:09:41.890
Ooyagi! Ooyagi!

00:09:42.310 --> 00:09:43.890
Ooyagi!

00:09:47.060 --> 00:09:50.060
I really don't understand today's Japanese students.

00:09:51.400 --> 00:09:54.610
Are you originally from around here?

00:09:55.150 --> 00:09:55.650
Yeah.

00:09:59.120 --> 00:10:02.240
It probably happened after I moved.

00:10:03.990 --> 00:10:04.790
Souma.

00:10:05.330 --> 00:10:06.120
Sou-nii.

00:10:07.120 --> 00:10:08.460
It doesn't ring a bell at all.

00:10:09.420 --> 00:10:10.210
Geez...

00:10:10.420 --> 00:10:12.840
That's not what you really want to ask, right?

00:10:13.800 --> 00:10:16.800
Sensei, what's your relationship with Mihoshi-senpai?

00:10:17.220 --> 00:10:18.380
So you know her too?

00:10:19.140 --> 00:10:20.050
Well... yes.

00:10:20.590 --> 00:10:22.720
We all belong to the Astronomy Club.

00:10:23.060 --> 00:10:26.390
That's not all, is it, Sa-ku-chan?

00:10:26.480 --> 00:10:29.900
Hey! Stop saying weird things!

00:10:30.520 --> 00:10:31.060
Saku?

00:10:31.770 --> 00:10:32.610
Saku...

00:10:33.110 --> 00:10:33.900
Saku... Saku...

00:10:34.530 --> 00:10:37.030
Saku... Saku...

00:10:38.740 --> 00:10:39.280
Oh...

00:10:39.910 --> 00:10:40.820
Ah!

00:10:40.950 --> 00:10:41.870
I see.

00:10:41.950 --> 00:10:42.830
So, you're...

00:10:43.530 --> 00:10:44.910
What is it now?

00:10:45.490 --> 00:10:46.290
Don't worry. It's nothing.

00:10:46.910 --> 00:10:48.250
I see. I see.

00:10:49.500 --> 00:10:50.620
It's a nice name.

00:10:52.330 --> 00:10:54.670
This feeling... it reminds me of someone...

00:10:56.380 --> 00:10:57.590
The bell's going to ring soon.

00:10:58.300 --> 00:11:00.760
I'm sorry, but can you distribute these to everyone?

00:11:01.180 --> 00:11:01.510
What?

00:11:02.140 --> 00:11:03.260
But we're almost there...

00:11:03.510 --> 00:11:06.470
If I don't hurry, she'll come from heaven to pick me up.

00:11:06.930 --> 00:11:07.140
What?

00:11:13.020 --> 00:11:15.730
Sou-nii!

00:11:14.900 --> 00:11:15.770
Perfect timing.

00:11:20.700 --> 00:11:23.910
Sou-nii's a meanie. He left without saying a word.

00:11:24.410 --> 00:11:26.540
Now, now. Don't be depressed.

00:11:26.700 --> 00:11:28.790
We're in the same school, so you'll definitely see him soon.

00:11:29.500 --> 00:11:31.330
Sayo-senpai, do you know him too?

00:11:31.870 --> 00:11:32.210
Yup.

00:11:33.170 --> 00:11:36.090
Men run when they're being chased...

00:11:36.590 --> 00:11:38.710
Do you even understand what you're saying?

00:11:44.430 --> 00:11:44.850
Hey.

00:11:46.680 --> 00:11:47.680
Sou-nii!

00:11:48.810 --> 00:11:53.100
Starting today, I'm a teacher at this school and the advisor for the Astronomy Club.

00:12:00.360 --> 00:12:02.700
Souma onii-san...

00:12:03.240 --> 00:12:04.370
Souma-sensei...

00:12:05.410 --> 00:12:08.080
He's the Astronomy Club's advisor?

00:12:10.910 --> 00:12:13.670
Sou-nii!

00:12:20.800 --> 00:12:23.630
Geez... you're so short. I can't see you.

00:12:32.020 --> 00:12:33.940
When did you come back?

00:12:34.350 --> 00:12:35.980
You surprised me!

00:12:38.900 --> 00:12:40.730
I'm also surprised.

00:12:41.280 --> 00:12:42.610
I just came back last week.

00:12:43.150 --> 00:12:44.530
I've yet to unpack.

00:12:45.410 --> 00:12:48.830
I was planning to say hello to your father.

00:12:49.450 --> 00:12:51.330
Now, now, don't cry.

00:12:54.040 --> 00:12:56.290
It's been a while, Souma onii-san-

00:12:56.670 --> 00:12:57.630
Souma-sensei.

00:12:57.920 --> 00:12:58.130
Hm?

00:12:58.630 --> 00:12:59.250
It's me, Sayo.

00:12:59.630 --> 00:13:00.380
Yarai Sayo.

00:13:00.840 --> 00:13:02.090
Oh, Sayo-chan.

00:13:02.300 --> 00:13:03.630
Your hair's much longer.

00:13:04.130 --> 00:13:05.800
Can I ask you out in five years time?

00:13:05.840 --> 00:13:06.510
Nope.

00:13:07.890 --> 00:13:10.100
Say hello to Mihoshi's father?

00:13:10.930 --> 00:13:14.270
Mihoshi-chan's father, Professor Akeno Kazuomi.

00:13:15.440 --> 00:13:17.060
He's a university professor to whom I'm indebted.

00:13:18.980 --> 00:13:20.110
Man!

00:13:20.650 --> 00:13:24.030
So, she's just your university professor's daughter?

00:13:24.360 --> 00:13:25.240
Well, yeah.

00:13:26.280 --> 00:13:29.830
Professor Akeno was the advisor for the Astronomy Club.

00:13:31.290 --> 00:13:35.830
Normally, club advisors are just names and don't turn up,

00:13:36.670 --> 00:13:39.630
but he would join the students on their activities.

00:13:40.750 --> 00:13:44.170
I joined the club halfway through the year, but I had a lot of fun.

00:13:46.300 --> 00:13:48.090
I'm indebted to him outside of school too.

00:13:49.760 --> 00:13:52.060
You used to play with us a lot.

00:13:52.350 --> 00:13:53.470
It brings back memories.

00:13:52.390 --> 00:13:53.930
Camp!!!

00:13:52.390 --> 00:13:53.930
Nail diagonally

00:13:54.140 --> 00:13:55.980
I had a lot of fun too.

00:13:56.440 --> 00:13:57.190
Really?

00:13:59.150 --> 00:13:59.690
Well then,

00:14:02.610 --> 00:14:04.070
I'm your new advisor,

00:14:04.860 --> 00:14:06.610
so I'll do what I can.

00:14:09.030 --> 00:14:10.620
R-Rope!

00:14:10.910 --> 00:14:12.120
W-What are you-

00:14:12.790 --> 00:14:15.120
Oh my, a measuring tape?

00:14:20.250 --> 00:14:22.040
Yup, it's definitely narrow.

00:14:22.290 --> 00:14:22.880
What?

00:14:23.380 --> 00:14:24.090
I'm talking about the dome.

00:14:26.510 --> 00:14:27.760
Our event for the cultural festival.

00:14:28.470 --> 00:14:29.680
A hand-made planetarium.

00:14:30.140 --> 00:14:31.050
What?

00:14:31.720 --> 00:14:33.140
Is it really that surprising?

00:14:33.810 --> 00:14:36.270
Up until last year, we've only ever displayed minerals.

00:14:36.680 --> 00:14:38.980
Our planet models were only partially made.

00:14:39.520 --> 00:14:42.690
I've heard all about your small and weak club activities in the staff room.

00:14:43.520 --> 00:14:44.820
And about this cultural festival too.

00:14:45.150 --> 00:14:54.870
Details for the event competition

00:14:45.610 --> 00:14:46.990
What's important is this.

00:14:47.690 --> 00:14:48.740
The best event competition.

00:14:49.700 --> 00:14:52.160
They will judge all the classes' and clubs' events...

00:14:52.530 --> 00:14:54.330
...and prizes will be awarded to the top three.

00:14:55.450 --> 00:14:59.330
The prize awarded to clubs is an increase in club financing.

00:15:01.790 --> 00:15:05.300
Let's make this into a proper Astronomy Club that has a telescope by winter!

00:15:18.480 --> 00:15:20.140
They're being gossiped about.

00:15:20.560 --> 00:15:21.440
Doesn't it bother you?

00:15:21.940 --> 00:15:22.480
No.

00:15:23.060 --> 00:15:27.030
Pique

00:15:23.440 --> 00:15:25.820
Although it seems to have piqued everyone else's interest.

00:15:27.440 --> 00:15:29.740
But he seems like a nice teacher.

00:15:30.240 --> 00:15:31.660
His classes are fun too.

00:15:32.160 --> 00:15:36.450
I never said I hated him.

00:15:40.080 --> 00:15:43.130
You don't like this because a history teacher is directing things even though he just joined, right?

00:15:44.250 --> 00:15:45.840
Er... N-No...

00:15:46.300 --> 00:15:49.170
Say, say, Sou-nii, how were the constellations in the southern hemisphere?

00:15:49.550 --> 00:15:51.220
Did you see the Southern Cross?

00:15:51.510 --> 00:15:53.390
Yup. It was wonderful.

00:15:53.510 --> 00:15:56.010
S-S-Southern hemisphere?!

00:15:56.260 --> 00:15:58.640
The Southern Cross is also known as the night clock.

00:15:56.720 --> 00:15:57.640
President!

00:15:57.890 --> 00:15:59.850
What is it?! Is he all right?

00:15:58.680 --> 00:16:00.430
Since ancient times, it has been a favorite as the...

00:15:59.850 --> 00:16:00.640
...constellation representing the southern hemisphere.

00:16:01.940 --> 00:16:03.480
It's been seven years since I moved away from this city.

00:16:04.730 --> 00:16:07.610
In the first place, I only lived in this city for two years.

00:16:08.570 --> 00:16:10.110
Mihoshi-chan's father?

00:16:10.780 --> 00:16:13.160
Both her parents were busy with work, so...

00:16:13.700 --> 00:16:16.410
But if I remember correctly, he was a university professor.

00:16:18.540 --> 00:16:22.330
It's normal for people to have relations with others that I'm not aware of.

00:16:26.710 --> 00:16:27.340
Yet...

00:16:28.250 --> 00:16:31.090
Yet... Why does he bother me so much?

00:16:37.260 --> 00:16:37.850
Hime.

00:16:38.850 --> 00:16:40.140
Hey...

00:16:40.520 --> 00:16:41.680
How do you explain this?

00:16:42.140 --> 00:16:45.690
What? Explain? Nothing happened...

00:16:46.020 --> 00:16:47.480
That's precisely what we're talking about!

00:16:47.560 --> 00:16:49.230
What are you doing?! This is the perfect opportunity!

00:16:49.320 --> 00:16:51.990
Feigning innocence but in reality are secretly eyeing him up.

00:16:49.650 --> 00:16:50.230
Behold.

00:16:50.280 --> 00:16:52.240
The evil spirits are awakening.

00:16:52.400 --> 00:16:54.610
Besides, what were you doing during summer vacation?

00:16:54.860 --> 00:16:56.820
There's been absolutely no progress between you two!

00:16:57.200 --> 00:16:59.330
T-That's not true!

00:16:59.740 --> 00:17:00.740
Fine, show me your cell phone.

00:17:01.290 --> 00:17:02.330
Your cell phone.

00:17:04.080 --> 00:17:06.170
H-Here...

00:17:05.960 --> 00:17:13.920
Summer outing

00:17:05.960 --> 00:17:13.920
Aka-beko

00:17:07.080 --> 00:17:08.750
What exactly is this supposed to be?

00:17:09.170 --> 00:17:13.590
That's... the Aka-beko key chain... paired with Ooyagi-kun's.

00:17:13.920 --> 00:17:15.760
No!

00:17:15.930 --> 00:17:18.100
Edogawa-kun and all the seniors have this too!

00:17:18.300 --> 00:17:22.100
Don't be satisfied with having what everyone else has!

00:17:20.890 --> 00:17:22.930
Understood! I'm sorry!

00:17:23.930 --> 00:17:25.890
Hime, please try to understand us...

00:17:26.400 --> 00:17:29.770
We just want you to be happy.

00:17:32.820 --> 00:17:34.320
Therefore,

00:17:34.570 --> 00:17:36.200
go girl!

00:17:34.700 --> 00:17:36.200
go girl!

00:17:53.130 --> 00:17:53.670
Um-

00:17:54.380 --> 00:17:58.340
Ooyagi-kun, if you have any worries, please come and talk to me anytime.

00:17:58.430 --> 00:17:59.430
Go, Yukari! Go!

00:17:59.550 --> 00:18:02.220
Takanashi!

00:18:02.640 --> 00:18:02.720
Cultural Festival Committee

00:18:05.230 --> 00:18:08.060
The 38th annual Souei High School Cultural Festival.

00:18:08.520 --> 00:18:09.350
This year's theme is...

00:18:09.770 --> 00:18:12.070
Flight

00:18:10.730 --> 00:18:11.400
Flight!

00:18:12.770 --> 00:18:15.400
It means to soar high into the sky.

00:18:16.490 --> 00:18:19.110
The vast blue sky extends before you.

00:18:19.910 --> 00:18:24.660
Everyone, let's all work together and once more fly high this year!

00:18:28.620 --> 00:18:30.630
Cultural Festival Special Menu

00:18:28.620 --> 00:18:30.630
Flight Donburi

00:18:28.620 --> 00:18:30.630
Coming Soon!

00:18:31.130 --> 00:18:33.590
No! This is the one thing I won't give in on!

00:18:33.960 --> 00:18:35.760
Why you!

00:18:35.550 --> 00:18:39.260
Deciding on the Cultural Festival Event!!

00:18:35.550 --> 00:18:39.260
-Cafe wearing cute clothing
-Cosplay
-Haunted house
-Photograph

00:18:35.800 --> 00:18:37.420
It just has to be a café with girls wearing cute clothes!

00:18:37.550 --> 00:18:39.010
It's got to be the haunted house!

00:18:39.220 --> 00:18:42.600
A haunted house isn't even original!

00:18:42.680 --> 00:18:44.680
Neither's the café!

00:18:48.350 --> 00:18:50.230
I vote for the girls wearing cute clothing.

00:18:50.350 --> 00:18:51.810
Yay!

00:18:50.400 --> 00:18:51.770
Souma-sensei!

00:18:52.230 --> 00:18:56.320
Sensei, if we go for the haunted house, you'll become acquainted with lots of girls from other schools.

00:18:56.530 --> 00:18:57.900
And the girls will be wearing summer kimonos!

00:18:58.070 --> 00:18:58.400
What?

00:18:58.610 --> 00:18:59.490
That's not a bad idea either.

00:18:59.490 --> 00:19:00.700
Hey, Sensei!

00:19:01.370 --> 00:19:03.030
Take care of that too, okay?

00:19:03.030 --> 00:19:03.780
Sure.

00:19:08.120 --> 00:19:10.330
The cultural festival has quickly become the hottest topic.

00:19:11.120 --> 00:19:12.790
Even though we've still got little more than a month to go...

00:19:13.540 --> 00:19:15.840
Do you think we can really make a planetarium?

00:19:16.380 --> 00:19:18.300
I think so, as long as we get permission.

00:19:19.720 --> 00:19:21.680
He said he's looking for an open classroom right now.

00:19:26.140 --> 00:19:28.980
Looks like our class decided on the haunted house.

00:19:29.390 --> 00:19:31.690
The boys looked really keen.

00:19:31.850 --> 00:19:33.360
We need to do our best too.

00:19:33.650 --> 00:19:34.940
And in love too!

00:19:33.940 --> 00:19:35.360
Do your best~

00:19:35.650 --> 00:19:38.690
I have the Photography Club too, so I might be fairly busy.

00:19:39.190 --> 00:19:39.990
What are you guys going to do?

00:19:40.900 --> 00:19:41.450
Model.

00:19:42.320 --> 00:19:43.450
Model? Er...

00:19:46.490 --> 00:19:47.990
You were lax on the budget estimate for the gate.

00:19:48.580 --> 00:19:51.120
Correct it by tonight with the design team.

00:19:51.370 --> 00:19:51.830
Understood!

00:19:51.920 --> 00:19:53.330
Have you counted the number of black curtains?

00:19:54.040 --> 00:19:56.710
Make sure you keep an eye on them so that no one walks off with one without permission.

00:20:07.220 --> 00:20:09.850
A walking Cool-Biz.

00:20:07.220 --> 00:20:09.850
[Note: The Cool-Biz Campaign was introduced to curb power consumption by limiting the use of air-conditioning.]

00:20:10.100 --> 00:20:11.020
Don't interrupt her!

00:20:11.390 --> 00:20:11.810
We're going.

00:20:12.690 --> 00:20:15.190
Geez, you're really...

00:20:16.940 --> 00:20:17.570
Hey.

00:20:25.070 --> 00:20:29.410
Um, I'll tell you now that this isn't compulsory.

00:20:30.120 --> 00:20:34.000
As the Literature Club, we always publish our works we wrote over summer vacation...

00:20:34.620 --> 00:20:37.920
...as a Literature Magazine at the cultural festival.

00:20:39.250 --> 00:20:46.220
But some of them were created after our joint activity with the Astronomy Club, so it's a little different this year.

00:20:47.050 --> 00:20:47.760
Would you...

00:20:49.930 --> 00:20:51.100
...like to help out too?

00:20:51.600 --> 00:20:51.810
What?

00:20:52.270 --> 00:20:53.690
It's not compulsory,

00:20:54.310 --> 00:20:56.560
and you're allowed to prioritize your own things first.

00:20:57.480 --> 00:20:58.860
You can give me an answer later.

00:20:59.780 --> 00:21:01.990
So, can you consider it?

00:21:02.440 --> 00:21:03.700
O-Okay.

00:21:04.280 --> 00:21:04.650
Yes.

00:21:05.450 --> 00:21:05.740
Bye.

00:21:11.040 --> 00:21:12.790
W-What?

00:21:12.870 --> 00:21:13.790
What's with her?

00:21:14.410 --> 00:21:16.290
Ooyagi-kun, are you going to accept her offer?

00:21:16.920 --> 00:21:19.380
Er... it was so sudden...

00:21:20.710 --> 00:21:21.960
I have to help out at the Astronomy Club too...

00:21:23.970 --> 00:21:25.630
Oh, Saku-chan!

00:21:29.260 --> 00:21:31.260
Oh, looks like that makes everyone.

00:21:31.770 --> 00:21:34.560
Look! We've got permission for the planetarium.

00:21:34.770 --> 00:21:36.900
A member from the Cultural Festival Committee delivered it to us earlier.

00:21:37.100 --> 00:21:39.980
They said they'd let us use the Las Vegas room in Building C.

00:21:40.270 --> 00:21:41.150
It's huge.

00:21:43.190 --> 00:21:44.490
Now we can start preparing.

00:21:45.030 --> 00:21:45.450
Yeah.

00:21:50.780 --> 00:21:51.330
U-Um...

00:21:53.200 --> 00:21:57.500
Um, I've got some stuff that other people asked me to help out with.

00:21:58.830 --> 00:22:00.590
Can I help them out too?

00:22:01.000 --> 00:22:01.210
What?

00:22:10.430 --> 00:22:11.350
Saku-chan...

00:22:22.400 --> 00:22:26.780
I look up at the sky, and I think of you…

00:22:27.070 --> 00:22:30.450
but I can’t find the words,

00:22:31.580 --> 00:22:33.740
I want to tell you,

00:22:33.740 --> 00:22:36.250
but they just slip away…

00:22:36.580 --> 00:22:39.920
almost like Shooting Stars.

00:22:40.420 --> 00:22:44.500
In this Wave of Silence,

00:22:44.880 --> 00:22:48.880
a ray of light flickers the darkness

00:22:49.340 --> 00:22:54.180
playing with my memories

00:22:54.180 --> 00:23:00.020
and releasing my heart.

00:23:00.850 --> 00:23:02.980
Into the future,

00:23:02.980 --> 00:23:11.530
I will have these feelings again!

00:23:11.950 --> 00:23:15.950
No worries, I’m not alone.

00:23:16.200 --> 00:23:21.040
You have taught me I’m not alone.

00:23:21.040 --> 00:23:29.970
Listen to my “Twinkle” story!

00:23:30.090 --> 00:23:34.140
Maybe my voice would reach you.

00:23:35.510 --> 00:23:40.390
I look up at the sky, surrounded by Stardust!

00:23:44.900 --> 00:23:49.900
Next time: The Moon and The Osmanthus

00:23:46.110 --> 00:23:47.480
Next time on Sora no Manimani:

00:23:47.650 --> 00:23:48.690
The Moon and The Osmanthus.

00:23:49.900 --> 00:23:54.910
With Fuumin's invitation,

00:23:49.900 --> 00:23:54.910
Saku starts helping out the Literature Club.

00:23:54.910 --> 00:23:59.910
Everyone's feeling mixes together...

00:23:54.910 --> 00:23:59.910
It's so "blue smell" around here.
